					content: "The Mushroom Continent is the primary recurring location between Mario games. It is a large mushroom shaped landmass that features various biomes and serves as the hub world for the game. The continent is home to many familiar locations from previous Mario games, such as Peach's Castle, Bob-omb Battlefield, and more.",
